WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.325
A system writes a flawless refund instruction. It knows the account,

2
00:00:04.325 --> 00:00:07.815
the amount, and the command. Should the refund happen?

3
00:00:08.415 --> 00:00:13.286
That question separates capability from authority. Capability says the system can

4
00:00:13.286 --> 00:00:18.156
compose the effect. Authority says whether this principal may cause it,

5
00:00:18.156 --> 00:00:20.370
here, now, under this policy.

6
00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:26.574
Picture the task inside an authority envelope. The envelope names the

7
00:00:26.574 --> 00:00:31.159
principal, execution domain, operation, target, permission class, scope, ceiling,

8
00:00:31.159 --> 00:00:34.725
grant state, epoch, expiry, and required receipts.

9
00:00:35.325 --> 00:00:40.152
Those fields travel together. A plausible answer, trusted model, available tool,

10
00:00:40.152 --> 00:00:44.980
or high route score cannot silently fill in a missing permission.

11
00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:49.430
Our refund begins with read authority inside the accounting domain.

12
00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:53.665
The grant opens only the customer record named in its scope,

13
00:00:53.665 --> 00:00:56.360
and the read produces its own receipt.

14
00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.545
Summarizing that record is a different operation. It stays inside the

15
00:01:01.545 --> 00:01:04.880
domain, but transform authority must still be present;

16
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:09.465
knowledge access is not ambient permission to do anything with knowledge.

17
00:01:10.065 --> 00:01:14.212
Now the plan asks to send the summary to a vendor.

18
00:01:14.212 --> 00:01:18.360
The target crosses into an external domain, and the permission class

19
00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.245
changes from transform to disclose.

20
00:01:20.845 --> 00:01:24.438
The envelope lacks disclosure approval. So the message stops.

21
00:01:24.438 --> 00:01:28.830
This denial is not a broken system. It is a successful

22
00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.225
authority decision with an owned reason.

23
00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:36.515
An authorized approver may issue a narrower grant: this vendor,

24
00:01:36.515 --> 00:01:41.204
this summary, one dispatch, before expiry, with an effect receipt

25
00:01:41.204 --> 00:01:43.080
and independent observation required.

26
00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.128
Only then does the handoff compile into action.

27
00:01:47.128 --> 00:01:51.868
The dispatch receipt proves what was requested; the effect receipt records

28
00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:54.885
what ran; observation checks what actually happened.

29
00:01:55.485 --> 00:02:00.295
Now try a confused-deputy shortcut. A low-authority requester asks a powerful

30
00:02:00.295 --> 00:02:03.793
service to reuse the service's own broad credentials.

31
00:02:03.793 --> 00:02:08.166
The requested effect is possible, but the caller's ceiling does

32
00:02:08.166 --> 00:02:09.915
not travel with it.

33
00:02:10.515 --> 00:02:14.417
The envelope exposes the substitution. Principal, grant, target,

34
00:02:14.417 --> 00:02:19.781
and delegation chain disagree, so the deputy cannot convert its capability

35
00:02:19.781 --> 00:02:22.220
into the caller's missing authority.

36
00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:27.513
Time changes authority too. A valid grant can expire, be revoked,

37
00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:32.207
or consume its final use. A replay after any of those

38
00:02:32.207 --> 00:02:36.900
transitions must fail even if every model output is byte-for-byte identical.

39
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:42.031
Replacement is another pressure point. A better model may occupy the

40
00:02:42.031 --> 00:02:46.149
same capability slot, but it does not inherit secret handles,

41
00:02:46.149 --> 00:02:50.680
approval power, or a predecessor's live grant merely by being better.

42
00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.960
Permission classes make these differences explicit: read, transform, disclose,

43
00:02:55.960 --> 00:03:01.680
write, execute, and approve are separate powers. Convenience cannot collapse them

44
00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.760
into one role label.

45
00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:09.289
Missing authority should therefore be machine-visible. The result names the absent

46
00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:12.874
field, the denying policy version, the residual owner,

47
00:03:12.874 --> 00:03:15.115
and the lawful escalation path.

48
00:03:15.715 --> 00:03:19.741
This changes the meaning of useful work. A plan can be

49
00:03:19.741 --> 00:03:23.767
correct, a source can be available, and a model can be

50
00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:26.695
capable while refusal remains the only acceptable output.

51
00:03:27.295 --> 00:03:32.036
The repository tests a finite version of that idea:

52
00:03:32.036 --> 00:03:37.304
six authority fixtures, two pre-effect denials, one executed local effect,

53
00:03:37.304 --> 00:03:40.991
one observation, exact rollback, five revocation entries,

54
00:03:40.991 --> 00:03:43.625
and thirty-eight rejected semantic mutations.

55
00:03:44.225 --> 00:03:48.888
The formal model also keeps accepted issuance, dispatch, effect, revocation,

56
00:03:48.888 --> 00:03:52.618
one-shot use, and rollback inside the caller ceiling.

57
00:03:52.618 --> 00:03:57.280
That is real bounded support for the encoded transition system.

58
00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:03.057
It is not deployed authorization. Authentic identities, complete mediation,

59
00:04:03.057 --> 00:04:07.083
concurrent revocation, secure tool wrappers, production adapters,

60
00:04:07.083 --> 00:04:11.110
and open-world observation remain outside the result.

61
00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:16.645
So the chapter's core claim remains design rationale at argument support.

62
00:04:16.645 --> 00:04:21.131
The visual explains why authority should be explicit, versioned, revocable,

63
00:04:21.131 --> 00:04:24.720
and receipt-bearing; it adds no safety, transfer, or

64
00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.515
A S I conclusion.

65
00:04:27.115 --> 00:04:31.535
The refund stops or proceeds for a reason that can be

66
00:04:31.535 --> 00:04:35.954
inspected. Next, Failure Modes of Ungoverned Intelligence asks how such boundaries

67
00:04:35.954 --> 00:04:39.570
break, how we notice, and who owns the residual.
